{"ts": "2026-10-17T05:35:27Z", "task_id": "T-RENDERER", "attempt": 3, "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "failed_tests": 8, "real_execution": true, "applied_files": 1, "feedback": [{"file": "src/boardscan.py", "line": 31, "issue": "The diff creates src/boardscan.py from /dev/null, overwriting the existing implementation of load_projects. The task requires extending src/boardscan.py while KEEPING the existing load_projects unchanged. The new implementation fails 6 tests in test_loader.py (e.g., test_load_projects_returns_sorted_read_boards, test_load_projects_missing_root_exits_two) that were presumably green before this change.", "remediation": "Apply the changes as an edit to the existing src/boardscan.py, preserving the original load_projects function exactly as it was defined in the dependency task T-DATALOADER."}, {"file": "src/boardscan.py", "line": 80, "issue": "The regex pattern for parse_diagnosis is too strict: it uses [ \\t]+ to separate 'DIAGNOSIS:' from the cause, which fails to match valid input with multiple spaces or different formatting as tested in test_format_task_row_newlines_become_spaces / related diagnosis tests. The test failure indicates expected output includes a diagnosis line but the assertion fails.", "remediation": "Adjust the regex pattern to match the strict grammar 'DIAGNOSIS: <cause> (confidence=<confidence>) remedy=<remedy>' using a single space after the colon and handling the exact spacing required by the tests. Test cases show the format is 'DIAGNOSIS: <cause> (confidence=<conf>) remedy=<remedy>' with single spaces."}, {"file": "src/boardscan.py", "line": 58, "issue": "The parse_diagnosis regex may not correctly handle the cause field when it contains spaces or special characters, and the non-greedy .+? with trailing [ \\t]+ may not correctly capture the cause when combined with the requirement that the entire string must exactly match the grammar.", "remediation": "Refine the regex to ensure exact matching: '^DIAGNOSIS: (.+) \\(confidence=([^)\\s]+)\\) remedy=(.+)$' or similar, ensuring it captures the cause correctly while maintaining strict grammar validation."}]}
